NOTE ON THE THIRD-PARTY CORPUS

This licence covers the code, the generator, the dataset splits, the trained
checkpoints and the analysis scripts in this repository.

It does NOT cover third-party RTL, which is deliberately not redistributed
here. journal/artifact/fetch_corpus.py reconstructs that corpus by cloning
eight upstream repositories at pinned commits, and each of those remains under
its own licence: OpenTitan and pulp-platform under Apache-2.0 / SHL-0.51,
verilog-axis, verilog-ethernet and verilog-pcie under MIT, wb2axip under
Apache-2.0 / GPL, and BaseJump STL under its own terms. Consult each upstream
project for the terms that apply to its source.

The synthesized netlists under journal/corpus/netlists/ are derived from that
third-party RTL. They are included because they are what the reported numbers
were computed from, and a result that cannot be recomputed is not reproducible.
Anyone redistributing them further should check the upstream terms.
